and items - but I do understand your trying to find a way to make this Lost competitive in a werewolf game.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As for the Carapace - I'm not sure which kith blessing that you would have, but - per the book - it wouldn't matter. No amount of magic or trickery can avoid the drawback, so if the drawback involves wracking pain your regeneration wouldn't matter. If it's damage itself? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Well, none of the books have an example of a drawback inflicting damage after it's used - but personally, I'd say the damage would have to heal in the most natural way possible. No regeneration. No magical heal powers. The wounds were part of the price paid to activate the power, and if it is to heal, it should heal in the most natural way possible. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Regarding the Crescent, I still recommend you make it as it's default of a scene. Seriously, more than likely if your needing to use the weapon you'll want to use it more than once in a single combat and having it require being activated every attack means that more than likely, using it will end with you both Paranoid and Hunted.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As far as a time sink, it's no more of a time sink than if you got a machine gun and did the same thing. The reason for the recommendation to use those rules is because the option exists for people to dodge your attack, which means that against those individuals you'd have your full dice pool - and because really, attacking a larger sum of people would be more difficult than attacking a single person. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ultimately though, it's up to you and your crew what you consider to fit well with the rest of the group and it's game flow though. I think that's about as much as I can offer to assist with your request. Hopefully this helps, and if not well then um... well I got nothing :P </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm a bit miffed that the computer ate my post....So. Doing this again....<br /> The Alerting addition to drawbacks, is to give a scale. Hunted is just 1 huntsman or loyalist, who has 0 Tactical insight and is going in blind. The Mantle is giving away so much valuable tactical data. Like the sort of thing Governments put satellites into orbit and spend billions of dollars on, I'm handing out for free. When you think tactically knowing not just that someone is still out there but has 5 friends around them tells you when the best opportunity to attack is.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile while hunted sends 1 loyalist or Huntsman, Summoning every Huntsman from San Fran to Sacramento when I use my armor's power, or every huntsman in California, Oregon, and Nevada when I use my scythe's ability instead of just using it as a sharped piece of metal on a pole...is a lot different. There is no condition to resolve, just +1d3 or +3d10 huntsmen. So it really is just a matter of scale. Plus there are other drawbacks.<br /> Here is my Kith Blessing. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warrior\u2019s Challenge:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> When using Intimidation to issue a challenge to an enemy to target them instead of another they gain an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of the normal 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><i>Unbowed, unbroken:</i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the changeling\u2019s reforged body heals more rapidly than normal allowing it to face some truly staggering damage, and just keep going. The Changeling heals 1 bashing damage at the end of every turn, 1 lethal damage every half hour, and 1 Aggravated damage every 3 days. By spending a Glamor, once per combat scene the Changeling may reduce a number of boxes of damage equal to twice his wyrd. Aggravated become lethal, lethal become bashing, bashing become healed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh and the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dominance</span><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> facet is Lead the Lesser Pack it's the wisdom facet. It allows them to bring</span></span></span> someone int<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">o the pack for a day for 1 energy per person. Granting them 10 xp worth of bonus.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-26-2019, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T07:46:49-07:00","id":1337981,"title":"","content":"<div clas